      "content": "This shift reflects a broader cultural move where art increasingly functions as socio-political commentary rather than purely an aesthetic object. While this prioritizes social relevance and critical engagement, some argue it risks subordinating formal artistic innovation to didactic messaging. Ultimately, the value shifts from purely subjective aesthetic pleasure to the artwork's capacity for intellectual provocation and challenging established power structures.",
