      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're highlighting the difference between universal resonance and targeted polemics. Art rooted in transcendent beauty aims for a shared, non-verbal human experience, operating outside immediate political binaries. In contrast, explicit political messaging often requires shared cultural or ideological pre-knowledge to be understood, thus limiting its scope. This creates a divide between art designed for enduring contemplation and art designed for immediate mobilization.",
      "source": "target",
